203
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:42,000
So since 2000, as you're well aware, the city of Huntsville has established two financing districts as permitted under the Alabama Constitution to finance public infrastructure investments, the creation of district is a tool allows municipalities to promote economic development redevelopment

204
00:23:42,000 --> 00:24:00,000
due to public investments made within a TIF district. The principles very simple city makes public improvements to entice the read development of areas or the new development areas to increase the tax base that would not otherwise be seen without these type of improvements

205
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:12,000
being made in a nutshell. It says that this district without the inducement of these public improvements would stay relatively flat from a tax based perspective.

206
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:16,000
We've been very successful. This would be tip number nine.

207
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:30,000
Miss Smith finance director regularly gives you quarterly updates of those TIF districts, most of those have been closed out they've closed out early and brought new significant tax base, both to us Madison County and our school systems.

208
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:35,000
People commonly misunderstand what a TIF district means.

209
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:53,000
