390
01:02:36,000 --> 01:02:44,000
We drove Swancock Road, Councilman Maris' district, and the beauty that they saw is the different price points going up at Swancock Road.

391
01:02:44,000 --> 01:02:56,000
Great new subdivision, great looking full brick product, sign out front says starting the 200s across the street. Another says starting the low 3s. And then you've got bigger lots, 100 foot lots in housing.

392
01:02:56,000 --> 01:03:08,000
So that's the result of our affordability manager working, community development, planning and engineering, and urban development all working together saying how do we move the needle in affordability.

393
01:03:08,000 --> 01:03:16,000
We're starting to see that deployed on the ground. There's still a ton of work to do. So I'm proud of the effort that this team is doing on that.

394
01:03:16,000 --> 01:03:26,000
And you can actually drive by and see the results by price points and things that are for sale. And we're getting national recognition due to those price points.

395
01:03:26,000 --> 01:03:42,000
